  "note": "First election of the urban district council under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1898; poll for the whole town on Monday 16 January 1899, counted 17 January. The fifteen elected were the nominees of the Working Men's Unionist Defence Club; no party label is printed against individual names. \"Of the 2,700 electors on the register, 1,329 recorded their votes\"; twenty spoilt papers."
